{"name":"Diamond White","hex":"#e2eff3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"diamond","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A glimmering glass-like mineral that is an allotrope of carbon in which each atom is surrounded by four others in the form of a tetrahedron.","A gemstone made from this mineral."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or containing diamond, a diamond or diamonds.","Of, relating to, or being a sixtieth anniversary."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/diamond"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Diamond White","blocks":[{"text":"Diamond White is an American singer and actress. In 2012, she was a contestant on the second season of the U.S. version of The X Factor, where she became the ninth contestant eliminated in the competition. She voices Frankie Greene on the Discovery Family series Transformers: Rescue Bots, Fuli on the Disney Junior series The Lion Guard and had a cameo appearance on The Haunted Hathaways and has recurring roles on Sofia the First and Phineas and Ferb. She also provided the voice of Babs Byuteman on the 2019 Netflix series, Pinky Malinky. From November 2020 to July 2024, she played the contract role of Paris Buckingham on the CBS soap opera The Bold and the Beautiful. In 2021, she began voicing Lunella Lafayette/Moon Girl in the Disney Channel animated series Moon Girl and Devil Dinosaur, which premiered in early 2023."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Diamond_White.jpg/330px-Diamond_White.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_White","wikidata":"Q16240338"},{"title":"Diamond White (cider)","blocks":[{"text":"Diamond White is a brand of white cider produced in Shepton Mallet, Somerset, England by Brookfield Drinks, who bought the brand from the Gaymer Cider Company in 2013. Like White Star, it is a cider with an alcohol content of 7.5%. It was launched by the Taunton Cider Company of Taunton, Somerset, now part of Matthew Clark, in 1986, and is one of the company's major brands of cider. In 2015, Brookfield relaunched Diamond White with new branding, and launched Diamond Black, an 8% amber cider."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond_White_(cider)","wikidata":"Q18111842"},{"title":"Diamond","blocks":[{"text":"Diamond is a mineral form of the element carbon with its atoms arranged in a crystal structure called diamond cubic. Diamond is a tasteless, odorless, strong, brittle solid, a poor conductor of electricity, colorless in pure form, and insoluble in water. Another solid form of carbon known as graphite is the chemically stable form of carbon at room temperature and pressure, but diamond is metastable and converts to it at a negligible rate under those conditions. Diamond has the highest hardness and thermal conductivity of any natural material, properties that are used in major industrial applications such as cutting and polishing tools."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/Rough_Diamond.jpg/330px-Rough_Diamond.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diamond","wikidata":"Q5283"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Diamant_gisements.jpg/500px-Diamant_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Diamant_gisements.jpg/1280px-Diamant_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Diamant_gisements.jpg/500px-Diamant_gisements.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Main diamond producing countries (in French)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiamant_gisements.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Diamond_structure.gif/500px-Diamond_structure.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/Diamond_structure.gif/500px-Diamond_structure.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diamond unit cell, showing the tetrahedral structure","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiamond_structure.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Diamond_face_trigons_scale.jpg/500px-Diamond_face_trigons_scale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Diamond_face_trigons_scale.jpg/1280px-Diamond_face_trigons_scale.jpg?utm_source=en.wi